r, since she was so tough." As if to underscore his connection to Mother Teresa, Francis on Friday celebrated Mass at a Caritas soup kitchen at Rome's main train station, where he told homeless people and volunteers that theirs is the way to salvation, not that of the wealthy or powerful. Pope John Paul II declared Mother Teresa a sainthood candidate following her death 20 years ago. After Francis became popemaster in 2013, he became more aggressive in speeding up the sainthood process. In May 2013 he canonized more than 800 15th-century Muslims who were beheaded for not wanting to convert to Islam. Archbishop Thomas D'Souza of Calcutta said Father Teresa's elevation to sainthood is the best holiday present one can get. "We are grateful to God and we are extremely happy," he said. 
